==================================================================2600 1451   26
  Definition of Data                                              2600 1451   27
==================================================================2600 1451   28
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                2600 1451   29
==================================================================2600 1451   30
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 2600 1451   31
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       2600 1451   32
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 2600 1451   33
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              2600 1451   34
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   2600 1451   35
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     2600 1451   36
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            2600 1451   37
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  2600 1451   38
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     2600 1451   39
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     2600 1451   40
   calculates these spectra.                                      2600 1451   41
==================================================================2600 1451   42
  References                                                      2600 1451   43
==================================================================2600 1451   44
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 2600 1451   45
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   2600 1451   46
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 2600 1451   47
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 2600 1451   48
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 2600 1451   49
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    2600 1451   50
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        2600 1451   51
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    2600 1451   52
3) D.E. Cullen "A Survey of Atomic Binding Energies for use       2600 1451   53
   in EPICS2017" ,IAEA-NDS-224, (2017), Nuclear Data Section,     2600 1451   54
   IAEA, Vienna, Austria                                          2600 1451   55
                                                                  2600 1451   56
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library2600 1451   57
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   2600 1451   58
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   2600 1451   59
  of the data, etc.                                               2600 1451   60
